It measures and builds on third-party work, pinned in manifest.json:

- Laya model weights and the `laya` Python package, Convai Innovations / NandhaKishorM/laya, Apache-2.0.
  harness/predict.py mirrors the calibration and answer formatting of laya/agent.py.
- laya-mlx, mizorewww/laya-mlx, Apache-2.0. fixtures/parity/cases.json, state.json and questions.json are
  the port's parity fixtures (benchmarks/common.py::parity_cases and examples/); fixtures/parity/expected/
  are its published validation results. The timing boundary follows its BENCHMARKS.md.
- receptron/laya, MIT. harness/export_onnx.py follows its export wrapper and dynamic-shape setup.
- Workload text: public U.S. federal contract opportunity notices from SAM.gov's data.gov bulk extract
  (fixtures/workload/source.json records the file version).
